## Description

This detection identifies the execution of **rundll32.exe** using **Microsoft Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation)**.

`rundll32.exe` is a legitimate Microsoft utility used to execute functions exported by Dynamic Link Libraries (DLLs). While commonly used by Windows and installed software, it is also frequently abused by threat actors to execute malicious DLLs, bypass application controls, and evade detection by leveraging trusted Windows binaries.

Monitoring Rundll32 execution provides defenders with visibility into potential Living-off-the-Land Binary (LOLBin) abuse and suspicious DLL execution.

